Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)). The h7-platform codec sheet takes
only the PCM3060 (U3) core of OSCAR_AUDIO_01's Analog sheet: the mode straps,
the clock/data wiring and the supply/VCOM decoupling. It changes them as follows:
  - Mode straps keep hardware mode, ADC/DAC slave, 24-bit left-justified, but add
    DNF parts so the codec can be switched to I2C control: a 0 ohm from MODE to
    DGND, removable DEMP pull-down, a DNF SDA pull-up, and 0 ohm DNF links from the
    MCU I2C pins to MC/SCL and MD/SDA. The VOUT differential/single-ended choice
    (MODE pull-down vs pull-up) follows the h7-platform analog design.
  - RST is driven by an MCU GPIO instead of being tied to VDD.
  - Power: VCC comes from the h7-platform 5V_A LDO and VDD from the 3V3_D buck on
    the same board, replacing OSCAR_AUDIO_01's isolated DC-DC converters,
    LM317/LM337/L78L05 regulators and split grounds.
  - The SAI connector (J5) is removed; the codec connects to the MCU on-board.
  - Not used: the analog input/output stages, PGA2310, relays, jacks, pots and
    the power sheet.
